WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.200
Welcome to the Transhuman Daily, Saturday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.430
Here's what happened in transhumanism in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.120
Show your working!

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:21.250
An Anthropic mathematician says he and Claude cracked maths' most famous problem.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.790
And New York surgeons did the first transplant in

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.720
a trial of pig kidneys with built-in thymus tissue.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.910
OpenAI says its models improved parts of

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.180
AMD's upcoming flagship chip by up to 14%.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.160
But an independent tester found AI still trails people on judgement calls,

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.340
like designing useful research tests.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.400
In healthy volunteers,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.460
a Rutgers brain cap with an AI helper built sentences nearly twice as fast.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:58.140
And in monkeys, Chinese scientists found brain cells that track the hand in 3D,

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.450
handy for implants.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.900
On to longevity. In a first six-person trial,

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.540
stem cells put into the brain briefly improved Alzheimer's test scores.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.080
And in Sweden, a blood test matched a spinal tap at spotting Alzheimer's changes,

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.670
at least 90% accurate.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.060
Oxford's model says blood pressure pills prevent about

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.190
four heart attacks or strokes per serious fall caused.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.470
And in Finland,

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:28.500
a year of exercise training helped nearly half of over-70s on several fronts.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.670
On to wellbeing. In mice,

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:36.670
psilocybin or ketamine cut habit-driven mistakes, a clue to how they help.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.990
And across five studies,

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:44.150
people who found their AI companion attentive and non-judgmental felt less lonely.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.480
Now, the catch. NPR reports some people struggle for months after psychedelic therapy,

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.010
and trials may miss it.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.170
And Signal now blocks screenshots on phones,

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.500
to stop built-in AI agents reading your private chats.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.080
Out on the frontier,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.840
an implant that runs on blood sugar brought diabetic rats' levels near normal.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:09.750
In Tasmania,

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:15.910
Incat is building three electric fast ferries with 55 megawatt-hours of batteries each.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.790
And Delft physicists flipped the magnetic heart of a single atom,

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:22.110
in a way theory said shouldn't happen.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.470
An MIT expert re-ran the proof and calls it historic.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:29.620
Next, everyone checks. Show your working!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.550
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.310
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.340
That's the Transhuman Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.320
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
